def max_sum(arr, n):
    # Initialize the dp arrays for increasing and decreasing subsequences
    inc = [1] * n
    dec = [1] * n

    # Build the increasing subsequence dp array
    for i in range(1, n):
        for j in range(i):
            if arr[i] > arr[j]:
                inc[i] = max(inc[i], inc[j] + 1)

    # Build the decreasing subsequence dp array
    for i in range(n-2, -1, -1):
        for j in range(i+1, n):
            if arr[i] > arr[j]:
                dec[i] = max(dec[i], dec[j] + 1)

    # Calculate the maximum sum of bi-tonic sub-sequence
    max_sum = 0
    for i in range(n):
        max_sum = max(max_sum, inc[i] + dec[i] - 1)

    return max_sum
```

This function uses dynamic programming to build two separate arrays: `inc` for the longest increasing subsequence ending at each index and `dec` for the longest decreasing subsequence starting at each index. It then calculates the maximum sum of a bi-tonic sub-sequence by adding the lengths of these two subsequences (excluding the common element) minus one.

